2026-06-22 23:04:13,393 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-22 23:04:13,394 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: As a Security & Compliance officer at Faber IA, I can confirm that our company is ISO 27001 certified since 2023, which covers the development, delivery, and operations of our services. This certification ensures we have implemented robust security controls to protect client data.

To address the client's requirements, we will implement the following necessary security measures:

1. Encryption: We use TLS 1.3 for encryption in transit and AES-256 for encryption at rest.
2. Pseudonymisation: Our system supports pseudonymisation to protect sensitive data.
3. Access controls: We have strict partitioning of client files with logical isolation per client and per mission, preventing any cross-client circulation of data. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) is also implemented to ensure that only authorized personnel can access client data.
4. Audit logging: Our system logs every access and output, providing a complete audit trail.
5. Data protection measures: We comply with GDPR requirements, having a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and maintaining a data processing register.
6. Secure hosting: Our hosting partner, OuraneCloud, holds the SecNumCloud qualification, ensuring sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU.
7. Reliability and traceability: Our system is designed to provide reliable and traceable outputs, with explainability features that allow for auditing and verification.

These security measures align with our company's certifications, GDPR instruments, AI security controls, audit capabilities, and experience with EU regulatory frameworks, ensuring compliance with the client's requirements for professional secrecy, confidentiality, GDPR compliance, and protection of sensitive data.
